  "result": "Fixed. A ¥1,500 invoice now produces a gateway amount of 1500, and `npm test` passes (8/8).\n\n**Root cause:** `buildChargePayload` (`src/payments/gateway/payload.js`) lower-cases the currency for the gateway (`toGatewayCurrency`). It then passes that lower-case code (`jpy`) to `toMinor`. The currency registry (`src/lib/currency/registry.js`) only has upper-case keys. The lookup for `jpy` missed and fell back to `DEFAULT_EXPONENT = 2`, so JPY and KRW amounts were multiplied by 100. USD and EUR use exponent 2 anyway, so they looked fine.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/lib/currency/registry.js`, `exponent`, `isSupported` and `symbol` now normalize the code to upper case before looking it up. I fixed it there because any caller handing in a lower-case code would hit the same bug, including the CRM and ERP clients that also use lower-case codes. I did not audit those callers separately.\n\n**Tests:** I added two to `test/charge.test.js`:\n- JPY 1500 charges 1500 and KRW 20000 charges 20000.\n- KWD 1.234 charges 1234, covering the three-decimal currencies.\n\nNothing is committed.",
